Supreme People's Court

Opinions on the Coordination of Case Filing, Trial, and Enforcement Work of the People's Courts

Fa Fa [2018] No. 9

In order to further clarify the work responsibilities of internal division of labor and cooperation within the People's Courts, to promote the smooth connection and efficient operation of case filing, trial, and enforcement work, and to ensure that the parties concerned realize their lawful rights and interests in a timely manner, these Opinions are formulated in accordance with the provisions of relevant laws such as the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, and the Administrative Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China.

I. Case Filing Work

1. When accepting filing materials, the case filing department shall issue a litigation risk warning letter, inform the parties of the litigation risks, give necessary explanations regarding the application for property preservation, inform the parties of the specific procedures, guarantee methods, and risk bearing and other information for applying for property preservation, and guide the parties to promptly apply to the People's Court for preservation.

When accepting materials for applying for enforcement, the case filing department shall issue an enforcement risk warning letter, informing the applicant for enforcement of the obligation to provide property leads to the People's Court, as well as the risk of inability to enforce due to a lack of property available for enforcement.

2. When filing a case, the case filing department shall share information with the enforcement authority and properly complete the collection of the following information:

(1) time of case filing;

(2) name, gender, ethnicity, date of birth, and identity document number of the party;

(3) name, legal representative or principal responsible person, uniform social credit code or organization code of the party;

(4) address for service;

(5) preservation information;

(6) telephone number and other contact information of the party;

(7) other information that should be collected.

When filing a case, the case filing department shall fully collect the information of the plaintiff or the applicant for enforcement set forth in the preceding paragraph and remind the plaintiff or the applicant for enforcement to provide, to the extent possible, the information of the defendant or the person subject to enforcement set forth in the preceding paragraph.

3. When filing an enforcement case, if the person subject to enforcement is an individual industrial or commercial household with a trade name, the case filing department shall list the operator of such individual industrial or commercial household indicated in the effective legal instrument as a co-person subject to enforcement.

4. When conducting case filing review for the transfer of the property-related part of a criminal judgment for enforcement, the case filing department shall focus on reviewing the following contents indicated in the Transfer for Enforcement Form:

(1) basic information of the person subject to enforcement and the victim;

(2) property status or property leads already discovered;

(3) circumstances of the property transferred with the case and the property already disposed of;

(4) circumstances of the seized, impounded, or frozen property;

(5) time of transfer for enforcement;

(6) other circumstances that need to be explained.

If the information contained in the Transfer for Enforcement Form is incomplete, the criminal trial department shall be requested to supplement it promptly.

5. After accepting cases involving enforcement, such as applications to set aside an arbitral award, actions against enforcement objections, actions against objections to changes or additions of parties subject to enforcement, actions against objections to participation in distribution, and actions for performance of enforcement settlement agreements, the case filing department shall remind the parties to promptly inform the enforcing court or the enforcement authority of the court of the relevant circumstances.

6. Where the People's Court refunds litigation costs that were prepaid but should not be borne by the party after the judgment becomes effective, such refund shall not be made by filing an enforcement case.

II. Trial Work

7. When trying a case, the trial department shall verify the relevant information collected by the case filing department at the time of filing the case. If the information has changed or the record is inaccurate, it shall be corrected or supplemented promptly.

8. When trying an action for confirmation of rights, the trial department shall inquire into the status of ownership of the property to be confirmed. If the property to be confirmed has already been seized, impounded, or frozen by a People's Court, the action shall be dismissed by ruling, and the parties shall be informed that they may claim rights in accordance with Article 227 of the Civil Procedure Law.

9. When trying cases involving the delivery of specific property, restoration to the original state, removal of obstruction, etc., the trial department shall ascertain the status of the subject matter. If the specific subject matter has been destroyed or it is not suitable to restore to the original state or remove the obstruction, the parties shall be informed that they may apply to change the claims.

10. When trying a case remanded for retrial by a ruling of the retrial panel that sets aside the original judgment or ruling, the trial department shall pay attention to examining whether the subject matter of the lawsuit has been destroyed or changed such that the original claims cannot be fulfilled. If such circumstance exists, the parties shall be informed that they may apply to change the claims.

11. The main text of the legal instrument shall be clear and specific:

(1) For payment of money, the amount shall be clearly stated. Where the amount of interest or liquidated damages needs to be calculated, there shall be a clear calculation basis, standard, and start and end times;

(2) For delivery of a specific subject matter, the specific information such as the name, quantity, and specific characteristics of the specific subject matter, as well as the time and method of delivery, shall be clearly stated;

(3) For determining inheritance, the name, quantity, and amount of the estate shall be clearly stated;

(4) For division of property in divorce cases, the name, quantity, and amount of the property shall be clearly stated;

(5) For continued performance of a contract, the content and method of the party's continued performance of the contract shall be clearly stated;

(6) For removal of obstruction or restoration to the original state, the standard and time for removal of obstruction or restoration to the original state shall be clearly stated;

(7) For cessation of infringement, the specific method of the infringing act, as well as the specific content or scope of the infringed right, shall be clearly stated;

(8) For determination of child visitation rights, the method, specific time and place of visitation, and the handover method shall be clearly stated;

(9) If the parties have mutual payment obligations, the order of performance shall be clearly stated.

Where the quantity of property in the preceding paragraph is large, a separate list may be attached after the legal instrument.

12. In civil mediation, the trial department shall examine the authenticity and legality of the intentions of both parties and pay attention to the enforceability of the mediation agreement. If the obligations can be performed immediately, the parties shall be required to perform them immediately.

13. The content of the part of a criminal judgment concerning property shall be clear and specific. If the number of property involved or victims is large and it is not appropriate to list them in detail in the main text of the judgment, a summary description may be given and a separate list attached. If partial confiscation of property is imposed, the specific property or amount to be confiscated shall be clearly stated. If recovery of proceeds or an order to make restitution is imposed, the amount to be recovered or the amount of restitution, or the name and quantity of the property, and other relevant circumstances shall be clearly stated.

III. Enforcement Work

14. If the subject matter of enforcement is a specific thing, the original thing shall be enforced. If the original thing has been damaged or destroyed, with the consent of both parties, compensation may be made at a converted price. If the two parties cannot reach an agreement on compensation at a converted price, it shall be handled according to the following methods:

(1) If the damage or destruction of the original thing occurred before the close of the final court debate, the enforcement authority shall inform the parties that they may seek relief through the trial supervision procedure;

(2) If the damage or destruction of the original thing occurred after the close of the final court debate, the enforcement authority shall terminate the enforcement procedure and inform the applicant for enforcement that they may file a separate lawsuit.

If it is impossible to determine whether the original thing was damaged or destroyed before or after the close of the final court debate, the matter shall be handled in accordance with item (2) of the preceding paragraph.

15. If the enforcement authority finds that the enforcement content of an effective legal instrument made by the court is unclear, it shall seek the opinion of the trial department in writing. The trial department shall make a written reply or make a ruling to supplement it within 15 days. If the trial department fails to reply promptly or does not reply, the enforcement authority may report level by level to the president to urge the trial department to reply.

If the effective legal instrument with unclear enforcement content was made by a higher-level court, the enforcement authority of the enforcing court shall report level by level to the enforcement authority of the higher-level court, and the enforcement authority of the higher-level court shall seek the opinion of the trial department. The trial department shall make a written reply or make a ruling to supplement it within 15 days. If the trial department of the higher-level court fails to reply promptly or does not reply, the enforcement authority of the higher-level court shall report level by level to the president to urge the trial department to reply.

If the effective legal instrument with unclear enforcement content was made by another court, the enforcement authority of the enforcing court may send a letter to the enforcement authority of the court that made the effective legal instrument, and the enforcement authority of that court shall seek the opinion of the trial department. The trial department shall make a written reply or make a ruling to supplement it within 15 days. If the trial department fails to reply promptly or does not reply, the enforcement authority of the court that made the effective legal instrument shall report level by level to the president to urge the trial department to reply.

IV. Property Preservation Work

16. The following property preservation cases shall generally be assigned a case number with the prefix "Cai Bao" by the case filing department for review and the making of a ruling:

(1) Cases where an interested party applies for property preservation before filing a lawsuit or applying for arbitration;

(2) Cases where a party, during arbitration, submits an application to the People's Court through the arbitration institution for property preservation;

(3) Cases where a party applies for property preservation after an effective legal instrument is issued but before the enforcement procedure commences.

For cases where a party applies for property preservation during litigation, the trial department responsible for hearing the case shall generally review the application using the case number of the litigation and make a ruling.

For cases where a party applies for property preservation after appealing but before the second-instance court accepts the case for filing, the trial department of the first-instance court shall review the application and make a ruling.

17. Property preservation rulings made by the case filing department or the trial department shall be promptly submitted to the case filing department for assignment of a case number with the prefix "Zhi Bao" for enforcement cases, and after filing, they shall be submitted for enforcement.

A higher-level court may designate a lower-level court to file and enforce a property preservation ruling.

18. The following matters in a property preservation case shall be reviewed by the department that made the property preservation ruling:

(1) Rejecting the preservation application;

(2) Granting withdrawal of the application, treating the application as withdrawn;

(3) Changing the preservation guarantee;

(4) Continuing preservation, lifting preservation;

(5) Permitting the person subject to preservation to apply to dispose of the preserved property on their own in accordance with Article 20, Paragraph 1, of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Handling of Property Preservation Cases by the People's Courts;

(6) The preserving court that first carried out seizure, impoundment, or freezing transfers the preserved property to the enforcing court that has the priority rotating seizure, impoundment, or freezing;

(7) A party or an interested party who is dissatisfied with the property preservation ruling applies for reconsideration;

(8) Other matters concerning the preservation content or measures that need to be handled.

After a preservation measure is taken and the case proceeds to the next stage, the receiving department corresponding to that stage shall be responsible for reviewing the matters set forth in the preceding paragraph. If continuation of preservation is needed after the judgment becomes effective but before the application for enforcement, the trial department that made the judgment shall make a ruling on continuing preservation.

19. The department implementing the preservation shall be responsible for handling the following matters in the enforcement of a property preservation case:

(1) Implementing, continuing, and lifting seizure, impoundment, and freezing measures;

(2) Supervising the person subject to preservation in disposing of the preserved property on their own in accordance with Article 20, Paragraph 1, of the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues Concerning the Handling of Property Preservation Cases by the People's Courts, and controlling the corresponding proceeds;

(3) Other preservation measures that need to be implemented.

20. After a preservation measure is implemented, the department implementing the preservation shall promptly notify the department that made the property preservation ruling of the property preservation status and transfer copies of the ruling and the letter of assistance in enforcement for archiving. Cases with the prefix "Zhi Bao" shall be separately filed and archived.

21. If the preserved property is not the subject matter of the litigation dispute and a third party, based on substantive rights, raises an objection to the preservation ruling or the enforcement act, the department responsible for reviewing the third party's objection shall review the objection in accordance with Article 227 of the Civil Procedure Law.

V. Mechanism Operation

22. People's Courts at all levels may, based on their internal institutional setup, designate the departments responsible for the coordination of case filing, trial, and enforcement work, formulate and refine the relevant systems for the coordination of case filing, trial, and enforcement work, and, in light of the characteristics of their institutional setup, establish and improve a long-term mechanism for the coordination of case filing, trial, and enforcement work within the court.

23. If a judge or judicial assistant, due to willful misconduct or gross negligence, causes a disconnect in case filing, trial, or enforcement work during any of these stages, resulting in difficulties in enforcing an effective legal instrument, the corresponding responsibility shall be pursued in accordance with relevant provisions.

May 28, 2018
